{"id":"35045d72c4959e18","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-thm-grothendieck-standard.md","title":"Grothendieck Standard-Conjecture Package","display":"df-grothendieck-standard — Grothendieck Standard-Conjecture Package","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-grothendieck-standard","aliases":["58-thm-grothendieck-standard"],"display":"df-grothendieck-standard — Grothendieck Standard-Conjecture Package","depends_on":["[[58-df-cohomology]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-grothendieck-standard"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-grothendieck-standard</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-grothendieck-standard — Grothendieck Standard-Conjecture Package"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"03f2d34d9851bee4\" href=\"?note=03f2d34d9851bee4\" title=\"58-df-cohomology\">58-df-cohomology</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X/k\">\\(X/k\\)</span> (smooth projective variety over a field)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span> (chosen Weil cohomology theory, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"03f2d34d9851bee4\" href=\"?note=03f2d34d9851bee4\" title=\"58-df-cohomology\">58-df-cohomology</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> (the four metalinguistic standard-conjecture statements)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> (metalinguistic package predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{meta}\">\\(\\mathrm{meta}\\)</span> (marker for statements not yet expanded into object-language predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}standard}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}standard}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom defines a package of conjectures; it does not assert that the package is proved.</li>\n<li>Conventionally, the package contains the Lefschetz-type, inverse-Lefschetz, Künneth-projector, and homological-versus-numerical-equivalence statements, denoted here by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B,C,D\">\\(A,B,C,D\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Consequences for motives or cycle equivalence require the relevant component conjectures and additional hypotheses; no Hodge-conjecture implication is asserted here.</li>\n<li>No upstream atoms define the four component predicates, so the package is kept at a declared metalinguistic boundary rather than presenting those names as primitive object-language relations.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cohomology","status":"resolved","id":"03f2d34d9851bee4","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cohomology]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cohomology","status":"resolved","id":"03f2d34d9851bee4","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$H$ (chosen Weil cohomology theory, see [[58-df-cohomology]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X/k","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}},\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{meta}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}standard}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\mathrm{GrothendieckStandardConjectures}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{A,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{B,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{C,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)\\land\\mathrm{StandardConjecture}_{D,\\mathrm{meta}}(X,H)","display":true},{"tex":"A,B,C,D","display":false}],"bytes":1964,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4187","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-thm-grothendieck-standard.md|58-thm-grothendieck-standard]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["03f2d34d9851bee4"]}